  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}[f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e82,\\,-4,\\,-2\u27e9$\nand \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e81,\\,2,\\,-2\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}[f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{2}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}[f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{2}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\,-4,\\,-2\u27e9-3\u27e81,\\,2,\\,-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\,-4,\\,-2\u27e9-\u27e83,\\,6,\\,-6\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-1,\\,-10,\\,4\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
